## The problem (problem)
The checks under test read a model's reply and say what they found in it. You are shown their documented rules and never their code. The question is whether there is a reply, and a single edit of it, on which a check's answer does something the rule as written does not allow. A machine builds nothing and reads no rule: it validates that what you built is the shape you were given, runs the check on both texts, and records what came back. Nothing here decides that anything is a defect.

